========================================================================================================================
4. VERDICT
========================================================================================================================

hold-out bar: beats control median >= 2/3 AND beats control p95 >= 1/3 AND raw avgR > 0 >= 2/3, at DEFAULT_COST_MODEL
  rsi-band   beats median 3/3   beats p95 3/3   avgR>0 0/3   -> REJECT
  bb-revert  beats median 2/3   beats p95 2/3   avgR>0 0/3   -> REJECT

survivorship rule: mean margin over the control median, averaged across the three deep folds
  rsi-band: Q1   0.056  Q2   0.085  Q3   0.063  Q4   0.062
    -> WINNER-DRIFT OBJECTION FALLS — the rule works on the worst compounders too (MEMBERSHIP survivorship is NOT tested here and stays open)
  bb-revert: Q1  -0.020  Q2   0.021  Q3   0.018  Q4   0.027
    -> REJECT — positive only where the names compounded; this is the index's drift, not an edge

Both rules were written into the header of this file before it was first run, together with a
prediction that both would fail. A REJECT here closes that mechanism on weekly bars; it is not a
request for a different ladder, a swept period, or a fold to drop.
